  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A variable line passes through a fixed point $\\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\\right)$ and meets the axes at $A$ and $B$. If the rectangle $O A P B$ be completed, the locus of $P$ is, $(O$ being the origin of the system of axes).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "icZoC",
      "text": "$\\left(y-y_{1}\\right)^{2}=4\\left(x-x_{1}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ksv0p",
      "text": "$\\frac{x_{1}}{x}+\\frac{y_{1}}{y}=1$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MiudF",
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}=x_{1}^{2}+y_{1}^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lCQ2l",
      "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{2 x_{1}^{2}}+\\frac{y^{2}}{y_{1}^{2}}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the equation of line be $\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1$ since, the line passing through a fixed point $\\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\\right)$.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_mat_a33.png\">\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{x_{1}}{a}+\\frac{y_{1}}{b}=1$\r\nsince, $O A P B$ is a rectangle, therefore the coordinate of $P$ will be $(a, b)$\r\nHence, locus of $P$ is\r\n$\\frac{x_{1}}{x}+\\frac{y_{1}}{y}=1$",
    "image": null
  },
